// Local.xcconfig.example — copy to Local.xcconfig and fill in the token.
//
// Local.xcconfig is the one build input that is not committed, because it
// holds a credential. With it, every build from this checkout ships fully
// configured: relay address from Relay.xcconfig, token from here, nothing to
// type on the iPad. Without it the build still knows the address and first
// run asks for the token.
//
// The token was generated once by integrations/mcp-server/deploy-railway.sh.
// It is in the relay host's environment (Railway → service → Variables) and
// in the Local.xcconfig of any previously configured checkout.
//
// Assign after any includes, never before — in an xcconfig the last
// assignment wins, and an include that re-declares the token empty would
// silently strip it from the build.

PENCILLOOP_RELAY_TOKEN = paste-the-device-token-here
